Package: gridHR
Title: Grid-Based Home-Range Analysis and Radial Space-Use Profiles
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
   person(
      "Norberto", "Asensio",
      email = "norberto.asensio@ehu.eus",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4536-5073")
    )
Description: Provides tools for estimating and exploring animal home ranges using regular spatial grids (squares or hexagons). The package includes grid-based home-range estimation, analyses of the relationship between cell size and home-range area and spatial connectivity, and location-based rarefaction analyses. It also introduces a radial home-range approach that examines how space-use intensity changes with increasing distance from the centre of the home range, allowing the spatial organization of animal space use to be characterized from the centre towards the periphery.
